<article class="env-lemma" id="06IJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06IJ">Lemma <span data-tag="06IJ">90.12.4</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ be a morphism of predeformation categories. Assume $\overline{\mathcal{F}}$ and $\overline{\mathcal{G}}$ both satisfy (S2). Then $d \varphi : T \mathcal{F} \to T \mathcal{G}$ is $k$-linear. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/06IH" data-tag="06IH">90.12.2</a> we have seen that $\overline{\mathcal{F}}$ and $\overline{\mathcal{G}}$ satisfy the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="/tag/06IA" data-tag="06IA">90.11.8</a>. Hence the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/06ID" data-tag="06ID">90.11.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>